<title>UK: RUGBY UNION-REDMAN CALLED UP FOR PUMAS TOUR.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-REDMAN CALLED UP FOR PUMAS TOUR.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bath lock Nigel Redman received a last-minute call-up on Wednesday to join England's rugby union tour of Argentina.</p>
<p>The 32-year-old forward, last capped in South Africa in 1994, replaces Garath Archer of Newcastle who withdrew on Tuesday with a neck injury.</p>
<p>The other candidate for a tour spot, Leicester's Matt Poole, was ruled out of contention by a wrist injury. The squad fly out on Sunday.</p>
</text>
